      explanation: "□ is ordinary multiplication, which is associative (B). Checking whether □ distributes over ◊: a□(b◊c) = a(b+2c) = ab+2ac, and (a□b)◊(a□c) = ab+2(ac) = ab+2ac; these match, so (D) holds. By contrast (a◊b)◊c = a+2b+2c while a◊(b◊c) = a+2b+4c, so ◊ is not associative (A is false), and ◊ does not distribute over □ (C is false)."
